{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BvPFojaHA82d2WqpCjtw22","type":"tool_result","content":"EXIT=0\nOK: the Rust .so exports every symbol the C .so exports\n### rust profile=dev   C flags=-O0\n### rust profile=dev   C flags=-O2\n### rust profile=release   C flags=-O0\n### rust profile=release   C flags=-O2\nALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED\n24","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45ba9b72-275a-4877-bcda-880545c9eef8","uuid":"ed0c4140-666e-4aee-b0d1-8812beeb56b8","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:22:45.777Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"EXIT=0\nOK: the Rust .so exports every symbol the C .so exports\n### rust profile=dev   C flags=-O0\n### rust profile=dev   C flags=-O2\n### rust profile=release   C flags=-O0\n### rust profile=release   C flags=-O2\nALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED\n24","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_cbryxvljznlwfyjlbkyinocndys4bvzck5km7psx6ovrgcsndrja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n## Phase A — mapped the surface\n\nThe project is a single C translation unit (`c_src/src/main.c`, 85 lines, one function: `main`) built by CMake as an **executable**. `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]`**, and the C has no `#ifdef`/CMake options → exactly **one** valid build configuration (verified by enumerating the `[features]` table programmatically in `scripts/verify.sh`).\n\nCreated in the crate root:\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D` on the C `.so` exports exactly `main`; the Rust `.so` now exports `main` too. Symbol diff **empty**, 0 undefined non-libc symbols (`ldd -r` clean), nothing stubbed.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 7 rows for the 7 distinct rejection conditions in the C (`argc > 4`, `argc == 1`, `end == argv[2]`, `start > len`, `end == argv[3]`, `stop > len`, `stop <= start`) + 15 generic-boundary rows (NULL `argv`/`argv[i]`, `argc == 0`/negative/`INT_MAX`, zero length, one-past-range, overflow/truncation, guard pages, broken pipe, closed stdout).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 30 rows over the axes the C actually branches on (argc shape, string shape, `strtol` lexical form, value relationships, **argv memory layout**, build profile), plus `VERIFICATION.md` tying it together.\n\nTo make FFI-level differential testing possible I restructured the Rust into `src/imp.rs` (pointer-faithful `c_main(argc, argv) -> c_int` that *returns* like C instead of calling `exit`), `src/lib.rs` (`cdylib` exporting `#[no_mangle] main`), and `src/main.rs` (binary; captures the real process `argv` via `.init_array`).\n\n## Phases B/C/D — 54 differential tests, all driven through the exported `main` of both `.so`s via `libloading` (plus process-level `execve` comparison), randomized with fixed seeds. Full matrix `{rust dev, release} × {C -O0, -O2}` passes.\n\n## Divergences found and fixed (Rust only, C never touched)\n\n1. **Dead-code assumption was wrong**: the original translation hard-coded `end == argv[3]` as \"never taken\". With an `argv` where `argv[3]` points into `argv[2]`, the C *does* print `\"Third argument must be an integer!\"`. Now reproduced as the same pointer comparison.\n2. **`exit()` mid-program** → replaced by returning the status, matching a C `main` (also what made FFI testing possible), and `argc == 0` now reads `argv[1]` exactly like C.\n3. **`SIGABRT` vs `SIGSEGV`** on NULL/unterminated-string paths (Rust's debug null-check aborts) → byte loads now use `read_volatile`, so it faults identically in every profile.\n4. **Broken pipe**: `driver <long> | head -c 5` exited 0 in Rust (runtime sets `SIGPIPE` to `SIG_IGN`) while the C dies from signal 13 → `SIG_DFL` restored in `main`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":336,"cache_read_input_tokens":208635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":336,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45ba9b72-275a-4877-bcda-880545c9eef8","uuid":"b223f217-3ed3-4a4c-962a-ffcf047cc31a","timestamp":"2026-08-17T22:23:02.136Z"}
